NIGHT_LOADED({"seed":1108,"generated_at":"2026-10-21T06:00:00Z","chain":[1,2,4,3,5],"frame":{"collector":"J.D.","intro":["You are the new assistant.","On the table lies a note from the collector.","The key to the front door is in his coat, and he has gone home.","The clock says a quarter past nine.","You begin to sort."],"note_table":"File twelve envelopes.\nCabinet five stays shut.\nLock up before twelve.\n— J.D.","note_final":"Well filed. Tomorrow at nine. — J.D.","card_desk":{"kind":"Legend","description":"In the Central Legend Archive there is a reading table with a green cloth, and on it a lamp with a green shade. Along the wall stand five cabinets with drawers full of cards. In the evening, when the others have gone, the assistant who worked late sits there and reads. Only the hands can be seen in the lamplight.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1936,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","teller":"the previous assistant","note":"Don’t read it. File it."},"trail_notes":["Not recorded by me. My previous assistant.","Same hand. He worked on into the evenings.","His last. No more cards from him after that.","This one he did not file. Nor did I."],"card_five":{"kind":"Legend","description":"There was once a new assistant at the Legend Archive who stayed on one evening to finish the filing. The collector had gone home. The assistant put four cabinets in order and then opened the fifth as well, though it was to stay shut. After that the assistant was never seen again. The cards lay neatly in order, and what the assistant saw there was ____.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":"tomorrow","teller":"J.D.","initials":"J.D.","code":null},"final_words":["nothing","me","myself","the assistant","the previous assistant"],"door_locked":"Locked. The key is in J.D.’s coat.","midnight":"The clock strikes twelve.","good_end":"Well done. Cabinet five stays shut.","nee":"No.","not_yet":"Not yet.","into_envelope":"Into the envelope.","archive_note":"You need not go behind the divider tonight.","finish_first":"Not yet. Cabinet {roman} first.","digit_note":"{n}. The number of cabinet {roman}.","digit_first":"Remember: the lock of cabinet V wants four of these.","found_notes":{"chair":"One is where I put it down yesterday.","lamp":"One is under the lamp. Don’t move the lamp.","coat":"One is in my coat. Leave the coat hanging.","typewriter":"One is still in the machine."},"floor_note":"That one does not belong in that drawer.","machine_continued":"— continued in drawer 3 —","reactions":{"reopen_filed":"That one was done.","stalled":"Hurry up.","read_desk":"I said: don’t read it.","typo3":"It is there. Read.","other_hand":"he is not coming back","five_shut":"Shut."},"citation":"Source: Dutch Folktale Database (Nederlandse Volksverhalenbank), Meertens Institute (KNAW), www.verhalenbank.nl"},"cabinets":[{"id":1,"label":"Omens","digit":7,"drawers":[{"id":"1-1","type":"P2","difficulty":3.0868,"rank":0.1503,"note":"No place. Somewhere between the other three. Pin it on the map.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"WEV002502","role":"target","render":{"description":"A pool in which a mill sank; a pool in which hay wagons vanished and in which a coach disappears after a voice in the water asked where the man is, for the time has come. A will-o'-the-wisp above the pool means that someone will drown or that a house will be built.","place":null,"prov":"Gr.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/45349"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"WEV002004","role":"helper","render":{"description":"A light above a pool is seen as an omen of an accident. Later a boy drowns there who had got drunk out of grief at being rejected by a girl.","place":"Mussel","prov":"Gr.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43322","original":"Achter de boerderij van mijn broer in Mussel was in het \"oal daip\" - de Mussel A - een diepe kolk. Zw. Tuin ziet op een avond boven die kolk een licht branden. Ze vermoedt een komend ongeluk. En dit komt.\n'n Poos later is er een feest. Een jonge man - G.D. - vraagt een meisje, of ze 's avonds met hem uit wil. Ze heeft er geen zin in. \nVan verdriet drinkt hij zich dronken.\nLater heeft 't kind spijt van haar weigering, want D. wordt de andere dag dood uit de kolk gehaald.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[52.955,7.03889]},{"id":"c3","story_id":"WEV006902","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Prediction that something will happen by a canal; people with a light were seen crossing a road. Later a drowned boy was carried home along that path in the evening.","place":"Vriescheloo","prov":"Gr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43572","original":"Veurloop.\nOabram zag nog meer. Wazzen es n poar jongelu, dei zoln troun-n. \nToun de haile boudel veurmekoar was, woln ze de meubels koopn in Winschootn. t Wicht gung dr op of en de jong zol den in Winschootn bie heur koom-m. Hai bedochde zuk en verdronk zuk in n wieke.  \nMoar, en hier gait mie t om, oal Oabram har al joarn van te veurn zegd:“Doar gunders bie de wieke gebeurt nog es n keer wat. Ik zai dr mensn deur t veld trekn; langs dei loane goan ze en koom-m bie dei boerderij oet. Misschain verdrinkt dr wel aine. Ik zai ook, dat ze n lichie bie zuk hebben.” \nEn net zo is t gebeurd. Bie oavend hebben ze de jong langs t zulfde pad van de wieke noar hoes brocht.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[53.06833,7.11389]},{"id":"c4","story_id":"WEV007506","role":"helper","render":{"description":"A prediction that someone will drown in a canal within a day comes true.","place":"Veelerveen","prov":"Gr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/44134","original":"Toun ze mit t knoal aan t groaven wazzen, moz dr in t leste nog n dam deurstookn wordn.\nWazzen verschaiden manlu bie aan t waark.\nToun kwam dr aine langs, bleef n rukje stoan en zee: \n\"Joa, 't is n mooi knoal worn; t is allaind zo jammer, dat dr binnen vaarntwintig uur ain in verdrinkn mout.\"\n\"Och, doe hest altied wat\", zeden de keerls, en zai smeetn hom mit n schop vol zaand noar de kop.\nMoar kiek, d ander dag, t luip teegn twaalf uur en de mensn woln gau eetn, zee dr n seldoat teegn zien mouder:\n\"Ik goa eerst nog eevn zwemmen heur, veur t eetn.\"\n\"Och, jong, blief hier toch\", zee ze, t is muide nait meer weerd.\"\nHai gung toch hen, mor is best verdronkn.\n\nAal dizze vertelsels binnen woar.\nIk heb ze zulf beleefd.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[53.05583,7.12778]}],"hints":["Three places are there already. The fourth lies between them.","Within 2 hours’ walk of Mussel.","Find Barlage on the map."],"lock":{"kind":"place","target_geo":[53.0125,7.05556],"radius_km":6.0},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c1","field":"place","value":"Barlage"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":null},{"id":"1-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.1466,"rank":0.2991,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ051006","role":"member","render":{"description":"A father warns his children never to walk in the middle of the road at night. After all, they might run into a funeral procession.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25083","original":"Heit woe noait lije, dat wy froeger by jountiid of by nacht midden op 'e wei roannen. Sels gong er ek altyd yn 'e berm lâns. Men koe ris tsjin in lykwein oprinne, wie syn sizzen altyd.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ112406","role":"member","render":{"description":"Because funeral processions need the space, it is best not to walk in the middle of the road at night.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/30112","original":"Noait mat men by nacht midden op 'e wei rinne, fanwegen in lykstaesje, dy't altyd paed ha mat en dy't dan wolris tsjin jin oanstompe kin.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ034606","role":"member","render":{"description":"You should never walk in the middle of the road, because you may be pushed aside by a funeral procession.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22678","original":"Der woarde ús al hiel jong leard, noait midden op 'e wei to rinnen. Hwant it koe gebeure dat der in lykstaesje oankom en dan woarde men oan kant set.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"ENGELB_15_003","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"About the existence of witte wieven (white women) and the spit in the doorpost.","place":"Geesteren","prov":"Ov.","year":1979,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/128566","original":"H.E.: Van de witn wiew he’j doar wa mangs van heurd?\nVr.Vr.: Van de witn wiew is ok niks van woar.\nH.E.: Nee, mer te geet ok um t verhaal, he. Joa he’j hier nog zonnen beuld, zonnen witn wievnbeuld. Ne, nee, nee (door elkaar heen gepraat, ze zijn het met elkaar niet eens)\nVr. [Wolberink, Jan]: Wat hadn ze bie ouns ok zegd, oh jee no valt mie t kenneke in zee Dat stun nog moal vuur joarn in de Twentse kraant. Als ik t met ene schoen had vastgebondn, gevondn als de ander gebondn.\nA.Ve.: ... t spit nog in n stiel van n nienduur nog zitn.\nF.Ve.: t Spit brengn.","lang":"Twente dialect","front":"description"},"home":"cab:2"}],"hints":["Look at the numbers in red pencil.","Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The card about Geesteren belongs with the White Women."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c4","cabinet":2},"on_success":{"trail_note":0,"unlock_cabinet":2,"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}},{"id":"1-3","type":"R1","difficulty":1.0963,"rank":0.0502,"note":"The clock has stopped. These three know the time.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ100119","role":"omen","render":{"description":"Some children are born with a caul. They later saw everything. They could foresee death, like my uncle, who had already seen the deaths of all seven of his children in the form of little coffins on the floor.","place":"Kootstertille","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"TM 2901","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/36754","original":"Der binne bern dy wurde mei de helm geboaren. As se dy helm nei boven ta fan 't gesicht lûke, sjogge se letter alles.\nIk haw in skoansuster to Westergeast to wenjen. Dêr njonken wennet in frou dy is mei de helm geboaren.\nIn omke fan my sjocht de dea ek foarút. 't Is in Wybenga.\nSawn kear hat er in bern forlern en alle sawn kearen hat er fan tofoaren de kiste oer de flier stean sjoen. 't Is in broer fan mem. Hy wennet yn 'e Westerein.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ111712","role":"omen","render":{"description":"The seventh of seven sons is born with a caul.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0489","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/29923","original":"Bontsje Keke wie mei de helm geboaren. De sawnde soan fan sawn soannen wie mei de helm geboaren.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ036709","role":"omen","render":{"description":"One of seven boys always has to get up at night to see things. He is clairvoyant.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0489","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22922","original":"Jasper en Jinke fan 'e Boelensloane hienen sawn jonges. Ien fan dy sawn jonges moest nachts ta 't hûs út om hwat to sjen. Dat wie Gerke Veenstra.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"}],"hints":["Read them again. All three count something.","The same number three times. That is the time.","7 o’clock. Set the clock."],"lock":{"kind":"clock_hour","hour":7},"on_success":{"chime":7,"digit":{"value":7,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}}]},{"id":2,"label":"White Women","digit":2,"drawers":[{"id":"2-1","type":"P5","difficulty":0.6258,"rank":0.0,"note":"The tellers contradict each other. Go by the oldest.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"HOL000404","role":"variant","render":{"description":"Seeing a witte juffer (white lady); playing at being a witte juffer with a white sheet around oneself.","place":"Ingen","prov":"Gld.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/209537","original":"Witte vrouwen . Bij de pas (aanplant van wilgen of populieren met onderhout van elzen en essen) (lag dicht bij de woning van de zegslieden) zag men soms een witte gedaante lopen. Maar sommigen geloofden niet aan de witte juffer, zo werd Han Briene er van verdacht, dat hij soms de kinderen bang wilde maken door voor witte juffer te spelen (hij deed zich dan een laken om) Enige jongens wilden met Jas Gaosbeek, een niet volwaardige zoon van een bakker, een grap uithalen. Zij sloegen zich lakens om en gingen wandelen op een plaats, waar Jas passeren moest. Deze ging er echter niet voor door, maar begon de \"juffer\", die hij het eerst te pakken kreeg af te ranselen. De andere jongens sloegen toen op de vlucht","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"HOL002208","role":"variant","render":{"description":"In the evening, mistaking a stick with a newspaper on it for a witte juffer (white lady).","place":"Ochten","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210065","original":"Er moet een witte juffer gelopen hebben op het Zand (fruitteeltbedrijf) bij het witte hek (dit stond op de weg, die tussen twee kolken doorloopt. Keuken, hij was toen 18 jaar, ging eens met een kameraad naar Eldik (buurtschap) om een vriend te bezoeken. Deze bleek niet thuis. Op de dijk op de plaats waar beneden het witte hek stond, was een stok met krant er om gezet, als teken voor de castreur dat er \"keujes\" moesten gesneden worden. Janus stapte tegen deze stok aan, deze ging heen en weer, de kameraad beweerde, dat hij een witte juffer had gezien en was van dit idee, ook de volgende dag, niet af te brengen","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"HOL002604","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A white maiden who asks the way throws a hat full of money and disappears.","place":"Tiel","prov":"Gld.","year":1964,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210163","original":"Berend, den dakuil (een Van Uden) smeerde de daken van binnen aan met kalk, vandaar dat hij deze bijnaam kreeg. Eens liep Berend op de Grotebrugse grintweg bij de Twaalf Apostelen (straatje) toen een witte juffer hem de weg vroeg naar het veer. Berend zei haar die en nadat hij dit gedaan had, gooide zij hem de hoed vol met \"Berliner daolder\". Driemaal was Berend dit overkomen. Bij het veer gekomen wilde Berend haar bedanken, maar hij kreeg geen kans daartoe: zij was verdwenen.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":null,"role":"summary","render":{"description":"In Gelderland an object was seen: ____. (according to the oldest recording)","place":null,"year":null,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","summary":true},"home":"2-1"}],"hints":["Look at the years.","The oldest is from 1962.","That card names an object. Which?"],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"a47ea58aec1d9efb","accepted_hashes":["1743ddb01f88ace2b9257daad332f51f8ed98bf42f1c6fbfc6c94210fd2a5a75","1d0795e979de1c5600360d42034ee69ac7a893d9869bd41f574127989d183117","312d5d675a6c9317c4f9a11345446f2d6392b111386d21264045b48e720159c8","39e77321070ded712ae6052471907409145d9a0d5cd0e9ea76c7d1374418b50f","79f5f8fac2e8b146ea3e7ed3863c647e52be6e8c917a09dde4bb6010ba7638c7","9f3ec7014494fd71cd8e420e320f251d7a6f153139f889806f00ccc307bbd18e"],"fill":"c4"},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c4","field":"blank","value":"typed"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"2-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.1405,"rank":0.5773,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"BROUWERS001303","role":"member","render":{"description":"Sighting of a headless woman dressed in white.","place":"Oud-Valkenburg","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"E.H.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/131805","original":"Van stropers, -----\nEen zekere S. is hier geweest --- een zekere Joep S. die deed niks anders dan stropen.\nDie heb ik eens horen vertellen dat hij hier achter in het veld, in \"der Maord Gieëlender\" (in 't Moord-Gerendal B [Brouwers]) een vrouw ---- een vrouw recht voor hem uit zag lopen ---- Zonder hoofd, ---- Zonder hoofd. En dat mens liep, hebt U niet gezien.\nJa, of zoiets nu waar is en of zo'n man dat nu maar fantaseert, dat weet ik niet, maar hij vertelde het voor echt.\n ------------\nplaats van handeling: Oud-Valkenburg \n\nvraag opn. : hoe was die vrouw gekleed?\nantw. vert. : zij droeg een lang wit kleed en liep op blote voeten. Maar ze \n zweefde meer als dat ze liep. Zo \n vertelde Joep.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"BIJLSMA007508","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Someone with a death's head and glowing eyes walking about at night on hands and feet.","place":"Burgum","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":null,"initials":"T.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/130658","original":"By de Burgemer tsjerke ware nachts in minske op hannen en fuotten om. Hy hie in deadsholle mei eagen as fjûr.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:4"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LINSSEN007503","role":"member","render":{"description":"A headless woman roaming about at night.","place":"Leveroy","prov":"L.","year":1964,"code":null,"initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208804","original":"Vrouw zonder kop. In de buurt van deze boerderij zwierf 's nachts een vrouw rond:\"de vrouw zonder kop\". Iedereen had schrik daarvoor en 's avonds waagde zich niemand in deze omgeving.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"EGGEN001705","role":"member","render":{"description":"Meeting a white woman floating through the air.","place":"Berg","prov":"L.","year":1970,"code":null,"initials":"C.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/207880","original":"Onderwerp : wit wijf.\nTijd : einde 19de eeuw\nPlaats : Berg.\n\nIch weit noch, tot in daen tiēd mèr 'n paar hoezer in Berg sjtonge. En dao op Bemele aan, al gaar gein.\nOppenen aovend, heldere maon, gein mis of gèt, kaom 'n oud vruike nao hoēs, in Berg.\nMèh zie waor kaom aan 't begin van de grwoatstraot (grote straat), dao huërt zie geroēsj in de buim langs de weeg. Dao waor geine wind, en toch roēsjden 't. Zie kraog al gèt angs, en wol vlot wiejer loupe, pes aan de hoezer.\nMèh zie haet nog kaom eine sjtap gezat, dao kump 'n wit wiēf aangezwaef door de loch, zwoa grwoat wie 'ne wollek. \nZie ging rech-op van den angs.\nDoe die versjiening euver waor, leep dat auw minsjke wat 't loupe kòs, nao 't iërsjte hoēs.\nEn van dao haet me hör nao hoēs gebrach.","lang":"Limburgish","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a ghost.","The card about Burgum belongs with the Ghosts."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c2","cabinet":4},"on_success":{"trail_note":1,"unlock_cabinet":4,"stack":["c1","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"2-3","type":"R2","difficulty":1.0093,"rank":0.2542,"note":"Something is written on the window. Don’t wipe it off.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ037017","role":"card","render":{"description":"Witte wieven (white women) have been seen at a haunted spot.","place":"Garyp","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22990","original":"Oan 'e Akkereed by de Brandsma-wei yn Garyp spoeken wite wiven, seinen se.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"HOL001804","role":"card","render":{"description":"Places where silent witte juffers (white ladies) appear.","place":"Lienden","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/209943","original":"Bij het Brakelse bos, ook in de laan langs de Tollenburg (deze boerderij ligt aan een bijna verlande Rijntak) zag men witte juffers lopen. Ze zeiden en deden niets, zweefden alleen de late wandelaar voorbij.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KUSTERS004002","role":"card","render":{"description":"A headless lady floating about in the evening.","place":"Helmond","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"C.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/207730","original":"In \"de warande\" zweeft 's avonds \"de juffrouw zonder kop\" Daarom ging niemand 's avonds door de donkere warande.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"YPFOE088","role":"sill","render":{"description":"A farmer has two sons. One cannot be got out of bed in the morning, the other has to do all the work. At some point he is fed up with it and wants to wake his brother up properly. In doing so he hits him on the temple, and his brother dies. The family moves away because they can no longer cope. The linden tree has kept on blooming. The murdered boy still haunts the area.","place":"Goutum","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0311","initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12173","stain":"two"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"KUSTERS001712","role":"card","render":{"description":"Witte wijven (white women) disappear because of the friars; much witchcraft stopped by ringing the Angelus and by prayer.","place":"Nederweert","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"C.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/46375","original":"Vroeger waren er ook witweefkes maar die hebben de Paters weggedaan. Trouwens door het Angelusluiden en het bidden van het Engel des Heren is aan veel hekserij een eind gekomen.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"KROSENBRINK00105","role":"card","render":{"description":"At the Hemsink farm in Rekken it is haunted and witte wijven (white women) can be seen.","place":"Rekken","prov":"Gld.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"G.J.H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/129093","original":"Een streek waar het niet pluis is, is bij de boerderij Hemsink in Rekken, op een stuk grond dat ’n Breken heet. Het spookt er en er bevindt zich een kuil, waar witte wijven te zien zijn.","lang":"Gelderland dialect","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"}],"hints":["Read it from back to front.","It begins with G.","Goutum. Lay that card on the windowsill."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c4","object":"window","text":"Goutum"},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":2,"card":"c4","word":"two","stained":"c4"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"]}}]},{"id":3,"label":"Werewolves","digit":3,"drawers":[{"id":"3-1","type":"P1","difficulty":1.1309,"rank":0.9121,"note":"All four name the same thing. That becomes the label. Don’t write ‘a beast’.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"EDJSL003","role":"card","render":{"description":"A farmhand tells his girl that he has an errand to run, and that if she meets a vicious dog she must give it her handkerchief. She does indeed meet a dog, throws the handkerchief at it and flees. During the meal it is seen that he has pieces of a handkerchief between his teeth. When his room is searched, the belt that turns someone into a werewolf is found. As soon as the belt is thrown into the fire, the farmhand, who was working far away, is standing by the oven trying to jump into the fire. After the belt has burned, the farmhand is released.","place":"Bladel","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1894,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"E.d.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/9505","original":"De weerwolf\nEr was eens een boerenknecht die soms een weerwolf was.\nDe knecht vrijde met een van de meiden, maar zij wist van de prins geen kwaad. Op een keer waren ze een eind buiten het dorp gaan wandelen. Toen ze op huis aangingen, viel de schemer in.\nOpeens had de knecht zin weerwolf te worden.\nHij zei tegen de meid: \"Ik moet hier even een boodschap doen. Loop jij maar vast door, ik haal je wel in. Mocht je een kwade hond tegenkomen, die je wil bijten, gooi hem dan mijn zakdoek toe. Dan heeft hij iets om zijn tanden in te zetten, terwijl jij ervandoor gaat.\"\nHij ging weg, en een poosje later zag ze een grote hond op zich afkomen. Ze gooide hem de zakdoek toe en zette het op een lopen. Het dier scheurde de zakdoek aan flarden en at hem op. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"BOEKV179","role":"card","render":{"description":"A youth is a werewolf. When he is walking with his girl, he feels that he is about to change. He sends her on ahead and warns her about a big dog. She must throw her handkerchief to it, and then the girl can flee. Later, however, she and her family see the pieces of handkerchief between the youth's teeth. Werewolves always wear a band around their waist. The farmer the youth works for burns the band. The werewolf still tries to get into the fire, but he is held back. When the band has burned, the youth is an ordinary person again.","place":"Bladel","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1896,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"G.J.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35060","original":"Van een Weerwolf.\n\nOp de Achterste hoef woonde indertijd een boer, en die boer had een knecht, en dat was een weerwolf. Op een eigenaardige manier zijn ze daar achter gekomen.\nDie knecht vrijde met een meid uit de buurt. Eens waren die twee samen buiten dorps (1) geweest en 't was al tusschen licht en donker toen ze op huis aan gingen. Ze waren al niet meer zoo heel ver van huis toen voelde hij een onweerstaanbare lust om weerwolf te worden; maar de meid merkte het natuurlijk niet. Hij zei tot haar: \"Ik moet hier eens effekens (2) van den weg af bij genen boer zijn; ga gij maar door: ik zal u wel inhalen. Maar komt ge soms een kwaden hond tegen, die op u aan bijt, gooit hem dan mijn zakdoek toe; dien zal hij misschien wel vatten. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"SINBRABSAG185","role":"card","render":{"description":"A young man is a werewolf. When he is walking with his girl, he feels that he is about to change. He sends her on ahead and warns her about a big dog. She must throw her handkerchief to it, and then the girl can flee. Later, however, she and her family see the pieces of handkerchief between the young man's teeth. This is how they know he is a werewolf.","place":"Bladel","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1933,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/46940","original":"No. 185. Op de Achterste hoef bij Bladel woonde indertijd een boer, en die boer had een knecht, en dat was een weerwolf. Op 'n vreemde manier zijn ze dat aan de weet gekomen. Die knecht vrijde met een meid uit de buurt. Eens waren die twee samen buitendorps geweest en 't was al tusschen licht en donker, toen ze op huis aan gingen. Ze waren al niet ver meer van huis toen hij een onweerstaanbaren lust voelde om weerwolf te worden; maar de meid merkte dat natuurlijk niet. Hij zei tot haar: \"Ik moet hier eens effekens van den weg af bij genen boer zijn, ga gij maar door: ik zal oe wel inhalen. Maar komt ge soms een kwaden hond tegen, die naar oe bijt, gooit hem dan mijn zakdoek toe; dien zal hij wel vatten. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"LYST009","role":"card","render":{"description":"A couple go for a walk in the evening. The boy has to relieve himself, but before he disappears into the bushes he advises the girl that if a beast attacks her, she should throw her handkerchief in front of its mouth. A dangerous beast does indeed come at the girl. She throws her handkerchief in front of its jaws and the beast tears it apart. When the boy comes back, the girl sees that he has remnants of her handkerchief between his teeth. She now knows he is a werewolf and tells him so. The boy disappears and never came back.","place":"Erp","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"F.W.J.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13223","original":"De Weerwolf\nEen vrijer bracht 's avonds z'n meisje naar huis. Onderweg zei ie: \"Ik moet even mijn behoefte doen. Als je in tussentijd een dier of zoiets op je af ziet komen, gooi het dan je zakdoek voor z'n kop.\" Toen de jongen weg was, kwam er een dier op het meisje aangelopen. Ze slingerde haar zakdoek voor z'n muil en het beest verscheurde hem. Even later kwam de jongen terug en hij vroeg zijn meisje of er iets gebeurd was. Ze vertelde wat er was voorgevalllen en terwijl keek ze hem strak aan. Toen zei ze hem: \"Ik geloof, dat jij het beest bent geweest, want je hebt de stukken zakdoek nog tussen je tanden zitten\" Onmiddellijk was de vrijer verdwenen, en het meisje heeft hem nooit teruggezien.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"}],"hints":["Read the four again. Look at what occurs in each of the four, not at what happens in them.","It is an object.","Begins with H. 12 letters."],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"a47ea58aec1d9efb","accepted_hashes":["0816c12fbac2f4b6d44a5dbaf1f5ec7cc48573573b8af13e5b9843f7410042b5","b77c2a3bc94064902d7d48bba949b65906189672e41cd0aaffe7a132606d568a","f44c4500af05442436ea7dcd1a668815f115aae2802527b461cca1e70520e8f1","fb91db7e695c934437eafd350c33005361f6e5443f6c94eb33961d261ba42ed6"]},"on_success":{"print_label":true,"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c4"}},{"id":"3-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.3078,"rank":0.9137,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ084112","role":"member","render":{"description":"One of seven girls is a nightmare and one of seven boys is a werewolf.","place":"Rottevalle","prov":"Fr.","year":1971,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/32830","original":"Se sizze fan 'e sawn famkes út ien húshâlding is ien in nachtmerje en fan 'e sawn jonges út in húshâlding is ien in wearwolf","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ101519","role":"member","render":{"description":"One of seven daughters is a nightmare; one of seven sons is a werewolf.","place":"Drachtstercompagnie","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/36981","original":"Ien fan sawn famkes út ien gesin wie in nachtmerje.\nIen fan sawn jonges út ien gesin wie in wjerwolf.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ085401","role":"member","render":{"description":"One of seven brothers is a werewolf. When he has one of his fits, you must throw him an old apron or something like it. He then tears it to pieces. If you see someone with threads hanging from his mouth, you can be sure he is a werewolf.","place":"Rottevalle","prov":"Fr.","year":1971,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/33002","original":"In wearwolf is in minske, dy forropt de boel. 't Is ien fan sawn jonges (7 bruorren). As er wer sa'n kuer krijt, dat er hwat forskuorre mat, mat men him in âld skelk of sahwathinne tasmite. Us mem sei, dan gebeurde 't wol dat him even letter de triedden ta de mûle úthongen.\nAs men sa'n ien seach, dy't triedden ta de mûle út hie, koe men der fan op oan dat it in wearwolf wie. Dêr koe men se oan herkenne.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"HOL001916","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Acquainted with people who can turn into werewolves; a woman sees a werewolf or the devil.","place":"Maurik","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":null,"initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/209980","original":"Men wist nog wel mensen te noemen, die de naam hadden te kunnen weerwolven. Wat ze deden, wist men niet.\nDe \"aauwe\" Roel moest de weerwolf of was het \"den duvel\" verdrijven. Zij zag hem komen en schreeuwde 's nachts: \"Daor heddum al weer\" (moet in Ingen gebeurd zijn, de \"aauwe\" Roel was de buurvrouw.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:5"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about the devil.","The card about Maurik belongs with the Devil."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c4","cabinet":5},"on_success":{"trail_note":3,"unlock_cabinet":5,"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}},{"id":"3-3","type":"R3","difficulty":1.1798,"rank":0.9744,"note":"When someone knocks: count. That card under the door.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"EDJSL012","role":"card","render":{"description":"A day labourer is returning home and sees a plough with no horse or man coming towards him. The plough changes shape: it is the smallholder, standing before him. The smallholder begs the man not to give him away.\nAt haymaking time the two men work together. When the smallholder is asleep, a mole comes out of his neck. The smallholder vomits litres of blood. In the meadow the remains of a calf are found; only a few gnawed bones are left. The smallholder dies. The priest has to come before the coffin can be carried to the churchyard.","place":"Didam","prov":"Gld.","year":1980,"code":"SINSAG 0804","initials":"E.d.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/9514","original":"Mol, de weerwolf\nEen keuterboer, die Mol heette, werd altijd uitgescholden:\n\"Bierpoep! Twee emmers vol snijbonen en nog maar wind!\"\nDat kwam omdat hij zoveel at.\nKarels, een dagloner, keerde 's avonds laat dwars door het veld terug naar huis, toen hij een ploeg zonder paard of man op zich af zag komen. Hij trok zijn mes, maar het ketste af op het ploegijzer. De ploeg veranderde van gedaante, en in de man die voor hem stond, herkende hij Mol.\nDeze viel op zijn knieën en smeekte hem niet te verraden. Hij zou Karels een mud boekweit en een mud rogge geven.\n\"Van jou, weerwolf, wil ik geen boekweit of rogge,\" zei de boerenknecht. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"LYST008","role":"card","render":{"description":"Every night at exactly twelve o'clock a farmhand takes a small hoop out of the lime tree. He hangs the hoop around his neck and turns into a werewolf. He roams about for a while and tears apart everything that comes near him. After that he becomes an ordinary person again. The farmer finds his behaviour strange and asks the priest for advice. The priest realises that the farmhand is a werewolf and advises the farmer to send the farmhand on an errand from which he can never be back home by midnight. On the agreed night the priest takes the hoop out of the tree at midnight. The farmhand is standing under that tree and sees everything. He flees and never comes back.","place":"Erp","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0803","initials":"F.W.J.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13222","original":"De Weerwolf\nEen boerenknecht kroop 's nachts klokslag 12 uur in de lindenboom voor de boerderij. Boven in de boom hing voor gewone mensen onzichtbaar een hoepeltje. Dat hing de knecht om zijn hals. Als ie uit de boom geklauterd was, liep ie in de gedaante van een hond weg en verscheurde alles wat hem in de weg kwam. Als ie een tijd zo rondgelopen had, was ie weer gewoon mens. Na een tijd was het de boer, bij wie de weerwolf in dienst was, opgevallen, dat zijn knecht nacht op nacht weg was. Hij ging naar de pastoor en die had het zaakje meteen door. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ096724","role":"card","render":{"description":"One in seven brothers is a werewolf. Werewolves tear apart and kill everything they come across. So you must throw him something, such as a cloth or a ball, that he can sink his teeth into.","place":"Buitenpost","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"TM 3107","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/36156","original":"In wearwolf is in man dy't alles forskuort. Ien fan sawn bruorren dy't op elkoar folgje is in wearwolf. De wearwolf makket alles dea as er de kâns kriget. Men mat him sokke tiden hwat tasmite: in doek of in bal ofsa, dêr't er de tosken yn sette kin.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"VVUNL049","role":"door","render":{"description":"Every evening after dinner Sjang goes out and does not come back until very late. One time they follow him and see him take something out of a tree, and a moment later he was a werewolf. The priest is fetched and Sjang has to produce his things. Out came a sheepskin and a red stick with a red ribbon; these are burnt in the oven while three men hold Sjang down. When everything is charred, he says he is freed.","place":"Kessel","prov":"L.","year":1952,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"J.N.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35588","original":"De geplaagde herder \n\n't Gebeurde op 'Gravenhof' te Kessel, tussen 1860 en '70. Sjang van de Maas uit Neer was hier scheper; een onnozele, rustige kerel, die niemand kwaad deed, en elke dag zijn schapen hoedde. Maar na een tijdje maakten de boer en de boerin zich over hem ongerust. Elke avond na het eten verdween Sjang plotseling en keerde pas heel laat in de nacht weer huiswaarts. Dit werd zo verdacht dat men op een keer de knaap stilletjes achtervolgde... Men zag toen dat hij tot de holle boom liep, even voorbij het Annakapelletje; daar nam hij iets uit. Na enkele ogenblikken veranderde hij van gedaante, en stoof als schrikaanjagende weerwolf met een geweldige vaart weg. . . …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ071310","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of eight sons was a werewolf. A werewolf could never eat his fill; he was always still hungry.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28045","original":"As der acht jonges wienen, dy't op elkoar folgen yn in húshâlding, dan wie ien fan dy acht in wjerwolf. Dat wie ien dy't noait sêd koe, dy't neat fan ûnpas kom.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"}],"hints":["Wait for the knocking. Count it.","An odd number.","3 times. That card."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c4","object":"door","n":3},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":3,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c5"]}}]},{"id":4,"label":"Ghosts","digit":4,"drawers":[{"id":"4-1","type":"P4","difficulty":1.7006,"rank":0.7126,"note":"Torn in two. The rest is in the box on the table.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"DYKFRIES2156","role":"top","render":{"description":"A farmer from Westdongeradeel regularly encountered a plaaggeest (tormenting spirit). The animal always walked home with him but did him no further harm.","place":"Goutum","prov":"Fr.","year":1896,"code":"SINSAG 0333","initials":"W.D.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/69345","half":"top"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ121115","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"A group of tough lads boast that they are not afraid of the beast and cheerfully set off for the haunted spot. The bravest of them is indeed not frightened by the big black dog that approaches him.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0256"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"GENDT078","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"After his death he returns as a ghost. The priest is fetched and prays until the ghost is in a little box. The priest takes the box with him, which becomes very heavy, and banishes the ghost across the water. Now the ghost can no longer come back.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0410"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ122406","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"It is a phantom animal. Strange things also happen at another place: people do not dare to go there at night.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0333"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ039903","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"One of them dared to approach the ghostly thing, but when he came very close, he walked back again backwards. The ghostly thing went backwards just as fast as he did.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0478"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"DYKFRIES2168","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Passers-by were pushed towards the water by an invisible force. When gaslight came to the town, the apparition went away, and the water has been filled in with earth.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0333"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CJ015103","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"As the man and his new bride are about to get into the carriage, his dead wife suddenly appears. She reminds him of his promise and the newlyweds undo the marriage. The spirit of the dead can only find rest once a promise made before death is kept.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0402"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c8","story_id":"KOOIJMAN1543","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"All sorts of strange things happened there: the potatoes would boil on a hearth with no fire in it. At night people also saw will-o'-the-wisps coming from it.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0478"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c9","story_id":"DYKFRIES2156","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"The farmer made sure he could always offer the animal a piece of rye bread. His maidservant claimed she would be braver and that if she met the animal, she would ride home on it. When she once met the animal, it put its front paws on her shoulders, so that the maid was forced to carry the animal's weight on her way home.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0333"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c10","story_id":"CJ112339","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The dead woman goes to the cupboard and holds her knitting in her hands. Her daughters know where they must take the knitting. When it arrives at its destination, the woman finds rest.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0402"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c11","story_id":"INZ00039","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"But the mocking voice of the mountain spirit is heard saying that the treasure can no longer be found. A girl promises to marry, and if the marriage does not happen, to give a barrel of oil for the sanctuary lamp in the church. She marries someone else anyway, forgets her promise and dies. Her restless soul returns, but a clergyman manages to banish the ghost. Her plaintive voice is still heard: they could have helped me, but they would not.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0410"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c12","story_id":"CJ054903","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"At first the beast follows annoyingly at his heels, but then turns back after circling him twice. The man was badly frightened by it.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0256"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c13","story_id":"CJ067505","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"after he died, and he comes at night in a long black coat and hat to the attic, where things got wild.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-1"}],"hints":["Read the top piece to the last word. What is mentioned already?","The bottom piece mentions ‘farmer’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0333. There are three with that number in the box."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c9"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c9"],"stack":["c1","c9"]},"found_card":{"card":"c9"}},{"id":"4-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.2961,"rank":0.8794,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"WOUDA001805","role":"member","render":{"description":"At the place where a monastery once stood, a headless man may appear on a dusky evening.","place":"Oudega","prov":"Fr.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"E.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/50539","original":"Op it gemeintehûs fan Wymbritseradiel yn Snits is in âlde kaert. Dêr stiet it kleaster Nazareth noch op. Dat kleaster is nou fuort. It stie oan de noardkant fan de dyk nei Heech, in 400 m it lân yn. De minsken fortelle: it spûke dêr. Winterjounen, sa in 't healtsjuster, koene jo dêr in man tsjin komme sûnder holle.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"BIJLSMA002801","role":"member","render":{"description":"At midnight there is noise at the barn door and the bolts turn out to be loose. In the morning the bolts are always loose.","place":"Joure","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":null,"initials":"T.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/130383","original":"Om 1870 hinne wenne famylje fan mefrou De Vries, in boer Rommert Steenbeek, op in pleats tusken Lemmer en Slijkenburg.\nDêr hearde men nachts om toalf ûre hwat rinkeljen oan 'e bûthúsdoar. Gie men der hinne, dan bliek, dat de skoattels fan de doar wiene. Moarns stie stéfêst de b[û]thúsdoar los, men koe der nea de skoattels op 'e doar hâlde.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"WOUDA001602","role":"member","render":{"description":"On a farm, knocking and strange noises are heard, especially in the front room. The noises stop as soon as it gets light.","place":"IJlst","prov":"Fr.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"E.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/50523","original":"Op ‘Eeskwerd’ wie wol nachts geklop en fremde lûden, foaral yn 'e foarkeamer. Op in kear wie Idske Sysling by ús útfanhûs. Wy soene de oare deis nei it ‘festifal’ yn Oranjewâld. Om tolve ure hinne, grypte se my by de linkerearm en rôp: “Hwat is dat?” Ik sei heit nei:“Dat binne de mosken yn 'e klimop en de wyn, dy gûlt troch de sinneblinen.” Mar it kloppe en gûlde en steunde de hiele nacht troch, sadat fan sliepen net folle kaem. It fremde is: doe it bigoun to ljochtsjen wie 't meiiens út.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"HOL003326","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"In the evening someone is jumped by a witch or werewolf.","place":"Tiel","prov":"Gld.","year":1965,"code":null,"initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210358","original":"Een ander verhaal uit de Nude: Iemand moest 's avonds de paarden naar de wei brengen. Toen gebeurde het eens, dat hem een \"teuverheks\" of een \"weerwolf\" op de rug sprong.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:3"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a werewolf.","The card about Tiel belongs with the Werewolves."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c4","cabinet":3},"on_success":{"trail_note":2,"unlock_cabinet":3,"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}},{"id":"4-3","type":"R4","difficulty":1.1339,"rank":0.4583,"note":"When the machine starts: let it type to the end. The rest is in here.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CBAK0151","role":"top","render":{"description":"An empty farmhouse is haunted; at night a light burns and noises are heard. Finally someone dares to go and look, and he","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1900,"code":"SINSAG 0401","initials":"C.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/8760","half":"top"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"BLECOURTNB0052","role":"half","render":{"description":"The ghost disappears when a drunk man tells him to put the post back in its former place.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0404"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ011303","role":"half","render":{"description":"Once a man rode past that old house at five to twelve. There he saw a very large dog. And suddenly the dog was gone again. But on one side there was a hedge, and on the other side water. Where had the dog gone? The place was uncanny and the man became frightened.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0478"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CBAK0151","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"sees four card players. When he asks whether they are people or spirits, they answer that they have been waiting for him, because money is buried there that keeps them from leaving. It is unknown whether the treasure was found.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401","stain":"four"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CBAK0513","role":"half","render":{"description":"The answer is that they have waited a long time for someone, that there is money buried of which he may have a third, and the rest must go in equal parts to the poor and a church congregation. Once the request has been carried out, the haunting stops.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"ZEEUW060","role":"half","render":{"description":"After his death he comes back to haunt. At the spot in the horse stable, where no horse can be kept, a later occupant digs up a treasure.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"VODA_032_11","role":"half","render":{"description":"After her death the woman came to haunt her husband. At the same time of day when he had refused to give her water, she came by and asked for water. The neighbours saw only a yellow patch in front of the window, but the man insisted it was his wife's face.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0434"},"home":"4-3"}],"hints":["Read what the machine has typed, to the last word.","The machine stops in mid-sentence. The rest finishes it.","The number is SINSAG 0401. There are only three in the envelope."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c4","object":"typewriter"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c4"],"type_line":"Told by: the previous assistant.","digit":{"value":4,"card":"c1","word":"four","stained":"c4"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6","c7"]}}]},{"id":5,"label":"The Devil","digit":null,"drawers":[]}]});
